From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Braumann <ripetitor@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:30:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: pm_domains: continue boot on set-idle/set-domain
 timeout

The BSP driver calls panic() unconditionally when a power domain does not
reach the requested idle/on state within 10 ms. During early probe on
ELTAY RM66 this aborts the boot before init runs, and the dev_err naming
the failing domain is lost because the FIQ console is not printing yet.
The dev_err paths already report the domain; return the timeout error and
let the system reach userspace for diagnosis instead of panicking.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Braumann <ripetitor@proton.me>
---
 drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)
--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
@@ -633,7 +633,6 @@
 
 	return ret;
 error:
-	panic("panic_on_set_idle set ...\n");
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -971,7 +970,6 @@
 	return ret;
 
 error:
-	panic("panic_on_set_domain set ...\n");
 	return ret;
 }
 
